d Syndicate's flagship, waiting in the storm's eye like a spider. 'They knew the route,' Pilot Juna Kael said. 'Someone sold the starlog.' The betrayal sat cold in their stomach."}, {'n': 4, 'title': "The Traitor's Price", 'text': "Pilot Juna Kael laughed for the first time in days. 'All this way,' they said, 'and we were carrying the lock, not the treasure.' Dr. Ilsa Venn was already calculating the wake-up sequence.\n\nPilot Juna Kael let them live, confined to quarters. 'the Void Syndicate trades in hostages,' Pilot Juna Kael told the crew. 'We trade in something better.' It was a gamble; the crew's eyes said they knew it.\n\nThe traitor showed themselves at the third waypoint: the signal officer, paid in promises by the Void Syndicate. They seized an alien engine core and ran for the escape pod with the Void Syndicate's ships closing in."}, {'n': 5, 'title': 'The Grid Awakens', 'text': "The duel was legend before it ended: two ships in the fire-light, neither yielding, until Pilot Juna Kael did the impossible — dove through the grid's own gate, which an alien engine core held open, and watched the Void Syndicate break against the shield they could not see.\n\nSilence, then. The grid humming. Port Andromeda safe below. Dr. Ilsa Venn put a hand on Pilot Juna Kael's shoulder and said what everyone was thinking: 'We live.'\n\nThe flagship came on anyway, and Pilot Juna Kael met it ship to ship above the burning sky. It was the Void Syndicate themselves on the viewscreen, offering one last deal. Pilot Juna Kael answered with the engines at full burn."}, {'n': 6, 'title': 'Home Signal', 'text': "Dr. Ilsa Venn was offered an admiralty and laughed in the committee's face. 'I have a ship,' they said. It was the highest compliment the crew had ever heard.\n\nPilot Juna Kael stood on the hull at sunset, watching Port Andromeda turn below. light against the void — the stars had taught it, and the crew had proved it, and the grid would remember it.\n\nAnd when the next distress call came — as it always does, out in the drift — the engines were already warm. There are always more skies. There is always Port Andromeda, somewhere, needing its heroes."}]}

